# Site plan

Output: `sites/<slug>/brief/plan.md`. Nothing gets built until Jake approves it.

Follow the **conversation rules** in `skills/intake/SKILL.md`: one question per message, 3–5 short lettered options,
**I'd pick …** with a one-line why, "or tell me something else", the "use your recommendations" shortcut, batching,
no unconfirmed-site recommendations, no unsourced competitor names.

## Step 1 — Draft the sitemap (no questions yet)

Start from the trade's "Usual pages" in `skills/intake/question-bank.md` and the intake answers (work mix, existing
site, learn-mode findings).

Core pages (almost always): **Home**, **Services** (+ a page per major service when there are 3+ with real content),
**About**, **Contact / Get a quote**, **Privacy policy**, **404**.

Industry pages, added only when answers or sources support them:

| Page | Add when |
|---|---|
| Portfolio / Projects + project detail pages | builders, remodelers, landscapers, painters with 6+ real projects |
| Our process | high-ticket or multi-step work (builders, design-build, roofing claims) |
| Financing | the client really offers it (named partner) |
| Service area hub + town pages | several towns with **real local proof** (a project, a review, or a crew who works there). Renewal-style city pages: local H1, local photos, local review, CTA prefilled with the town. Never doorway pages. |
| Reviews | 10+ real reviews; otherwise reviews live on Home/About |
| Equipment / Our machine | equipment is a selling point (316) |
| Maintenance plans / memberships | real plans exist |
| Emergency service | 24/7 is confirmed |
| Storm damage & insurance | real insurance-claim help |
| Available homes / lots, Floor plans | builders with spec homes or plan libraries |
| FAQ | 6+ real questions |
| Careers | they're hiring |
| Pricing | the client agreed to show prices |
| Gallery / Before & after | strong visual proof and no project pages |
| Partner/sister business | linked businesses |

Pages you're unsure about go on a "maybe" list. Don't ask about them yet.

## Step 2 — Show the sitemap (one message, one question)

Send the sitemap as a short indented list (one line per page saying why), then ask **one** question:

"**Does this page list look right?** a) yes, go page by page, b) add a page (tell me which), c) drop something,
d) use your recommendations for everything. **I'd pick a.** Or tell me something else."

If there's a "maybe" page that matters most (e.g. Portfolio vs. one gallery), ask about it in the *next* message,
alone.

## Step 3 — Walk through pages, just in time

Go page by page in build order: **Home → Services → About → Contact → industry pages**. For each page:

1. Draft its section outline (Step 4) using what you already know.
2. List what's missing for *that page only*: trade questions from the bank that affect it (see the "ask when" table
   at the top of `question-bank.md`) and facts its sections would show.
3. Ask the missing items **one per message, most build-blocking first**. Default for any fact: `null` (hidden).
   Phrase facts as a choice so "unknown" is easy:
   "The proof bar under the hero can show years in business. **When did Heartwood start?** a) tell me the year,
   b) unknown, so hide it for now, c) skip the proof bar. **I'd pick b** if you're not sure; it appears once you
   send the year. Or tell me something else."
4. Things that are **not build-blocking** (e.g. warranty wording, team photos) don't get asked now. Leave them
   `null`, mark the section "hidden until confirmed", and list them at the end (Step 5).
5. Move to the next page. Don't re-ask anything already answered in `intake.md`, `sources.md` or `site.ts`.

Typical just-in-time questions by page:
- **Home:** main action (call / form / book / text) → hero CTA + mobile action bar; phone (needed for Call/Text;
  if unknown, the bar shows Quote only); which proof is available (reviews source, photos).
- **Services:** pricing stance; any service that deserves its own page.
- **About:** owner/team names and photos (else an About page without a team grid); year founded; licenses/insured.
- **Contact:** form destination (Resend email or GoHighLevel), public address vs. service-area only, area served, hours.
- **Industry pages:** the one question that decides each (e.g. Financing: "Who's the financing partner?").
  For Portfolio / project pages, do **not** ask how many photos we have — use the crawl counts. If the harvest
  is thin, ask Jake only for missing mid-phase, before, or owner photos.

If Jake says **"use your recommendations"** during the walk-through, apply the recommended pick to every remaining
question, leave all facts `null`, and jump to Step 5.

## Step 4 — Per-page section outline (written into plan.md as you go)

```
### Home
1. Hero: full-bleed job photo, H1 in the shared container, one primary CTA + quieter Call | image: the ranked memorable photo
2. Trust strip (C18 / P1): rating, years, licence, associations — confirmed facts only
3. Featured work: Eppright big-photo + info card (C16) or Nature's Call one-big-plus-two-small (C17)
4. Signature / process / services (as planned)
5. Owners on a job site (C20) if we have photos
6. Reviews
7. Service area (with town-page links if they exist)
8. FAQ
9. Dark closing CTA band (C19) with the qualifier or short form + phone
```

- Archetype IDs from `skills/page-build/archetypes.md`; no two adjacent sections with the same archetype; Home uses ≥ 5
  *and* at least three layout shapes (split or full-bleed media, a snap rail or ruled grid, a manifesto or dark CTA — not
  five stacked card rows). Follow each archetype's recipe, including its motion.
- **Composition moves** from `page-build/compositions.md`: list them per page (Home ≥ 4, interiors ≥ 2).
- **Delight:** 1–2 client-specific moments for the *site*, named in the plan (not 3–5 details per page).
- **Motion plan** (A7): one hero load-in, one CSS scroll-driven signature, hovers; everything else still.
- **Layout default:** shared, centered container and consistent left edges. Asymmetry only in restrained,
  grid-snapped amounts (a split hero, an occasional offset image), recorded in the plan — never required,
  never wandering.
- **Work index:** with 6 or more projects and good photographs, default to the C32 horizontal portrait
  rail (five plus a sliver at 1440, 1–2 plus a sliver at 390, live counter, 1:1 scrollbar, prev/next,
  no scroll-jacking). Use a photo-forward C15 / W7 (photo-led list or split list with a sticky
  crossfading image; large mobile thumbnails) only when the set is smaller or the photos cannot
  support a rail. Not a typographic cursor-follow, and not a generic card grid.
  With 8 or more projects, plan job-type filters (C29) above the rail: All plus types the harvest supports, counts,
  `?type=` URLs, no empty categories, in-place fade.
- **Project detail pages:** every project page uses the **C28 shell** (photo-first opening, Walk through rail,
  reactive photos, save heart, next-house card). Each project in `plan.md` also lists its harvested photo
  count and the compositions it can genuinely support from C22–C26 (build-story, room-by-room, editorial
  spreads, same-vantage before/after or day/dusk drag reveal, detail hotspots). Do not plan a single-hero or
  typography-first page when the crawl found a gallery. Fullscreen is a utility only. See
  `page-build/compositions.md` and `templates/project-page.md`.
- **Primary service page:** the client's main offering (e.g. Custom Homes) uses C30 — photo-first, a
  compact how-it-works widget unique to that page, sourced inclusions, featured work, cost only with
  real numbers, FAQ, trust beside the ask. Our Process (or equivalent) gets the full timeline. Do not
  plan the same distinctive widget on two pages.
- **Home lot-to-finish scrubber:** when same-house phase photos exist, plan C31 (overlay scrubber:
  photo-as-control, glass bar on the media, branded track, no pinned or scroll-jacked scroll, primary
  CTA only at the last chapter). Not a tall photo with the range input and CTA in a panel below it.
- **Anti-generic:** do not plan eyebrows on every heading, fade-up on every section, or a count-up stat row
  unless each is justified by name. Do not default the palette to cream + serif + terracotta.
  Home's feature is the trade-specific signature interaction.
- Mark where the one **signature interaction** lives. On Home it belongs in the hero (H7) or as the first content
  section (T3), full width — not buried. If photos are still pending, the plan still includes it (placeholder frames).
- Note the first-viewport plan for Home *and* each interior page (H1/H2/H4) so no page opens on a bare heading stack.
  Write the site's one-sentence point of view into `brand.md` if it isn't there yet.
- Draft headlines in the chosen voice; every fact shows its source or `null`.
- Assets needed per section, and whether we have them.
- SEO per page: title, meta description, target query, H1.
- Existing site: old URL → new URL redirects.

Also write, in the same `plan.md`:

- **Funnel map (P6):** every page has a stage, one primary action (verb + outcome), a secondary, and its trust elements.
- **Tool evaluation (P7):** score candidates and apply Jake's rule — a quote or estimator only when the client can supply real pricing inputs; otherwise an Adair/Schumacher multi-step qualifier, contact last. List the data Jake must get if a tool is a placeholder.
- **Top objections (P8):** the client's top five, each assigned to a section or the FAQ. Ask Jake if they aren't in intake.
- **City pages (P9):** only towns with local proof. Skip if there is none.
- **Measurement plan (P10):** copy `templates/measurement-plan.md` to `brief/measurement.md` and fill the chosen analytics tool and the event list. Note the 90-day baseline and the monthly report template.

## Step 5 — Approval

Send one short message: page count, a link to `plan.md`, the list of facts that are hidden until confirmed
(one line each), and one question:

"**Good to build?** a) yes, build it, b) change something first (tell me), c) let me read plan.md first.
**I'd pick a:** hidden facts can be filled in any time without a rebuild of the layout. Or tell me something else."

Build only after a clear go. Then `skills/page-build/SKILL.md`.

